Death drops are the only way in the game to create "a random object"
from the full scope of all possibilties listed in the item spoiler
(along with dungeon level initialization). Only monsters actively
killed by the hero get those things, as opposed to pet kills,
conflict, confused in-fighting, traps, zapping bystanders, etc.

The spoiler makes it clear no monster can be generated with things
such as "a random ring", "a random piece of armor", etc. Monsters are
strictly limited to a subset of not-so-useful items. As it turns out,
this subset is quite limited, especially for things other than wands.

> "In addition these monsters might be eligible for a random offensive
> A defensive item is one of ...
> A miscellaneous item is one of ..."
[...]

For example, monsters will never be generated with wands of light,
enlightenment, locking, opening, probing, secret door detection, slow
monster, undead turning, cancellation, wishing.
The only scrolls monsters can have are teleportation, create monster,
earth. Only priests can ever be generated with spellbooks. The only
ring monsters can have is the ring of invisiblity on nazgul.

And so on.

> "Note that a lot of monsters actually produce some stuff when they are
> killed ..."

That confuses two different mechanisms: the predetermined items from
dragons, golems, unicorns, long worms, versus the death drops only
hero kills get.

